hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19650","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Yala ibn Ata from Umarah ibn Hadid al-Bajali from Sakhr al-Ghamidi from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: O Allah, bless my nation in its early mornings. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he sent an expedition, would send it at the beginning of the day. And Sakhr was a merchant man, and he would not send his servants except from the beginning of the day, so his wealth increased until he did not know where to put his wealth."
